# Secrets written by FileSecretManager (src/services/secret_manager/filesecretmanager.py).
#
# SECRET_MANAGER_DIRECTORY defaults to "./", so any local run that calls
# GET /settings/webhook or installs a provider drops PLAINTEXT credentials in the
# repo root, with no extension. The generated names are:
#   {tenant_id}-{api_key_id}              API keys        e.g. keep-webhook
#   {tenant_id}_{provider_type}_{id}      provider config e.g. keep_grafana_1
#   {tenant_id}_smtp                      SMTP settings
# In single-tenant dev tenant_id is "keep"; with real multi-tenancy it is a UUID,
# which these patterns will NOT catch -- set SECRET_MANAGER_DIRECTORY=./secrets
# rather than relying on them.
/keep-*
/keep_*
/*_smtp
/secrets/
